      "round_summary": "Repair round 2/2: Fix mutex_ack by modifying Controller.BUSY exit condition (lines 85-86). Added `!is_selected` guard so a controller de-asserts ack when the arbiter cycles past its selection slot, preventing simultaneous ack assertions. Root cause: anyReq override (round 1 fix) keeps arbiter cycling through clients even while a controller is BUSY with ack high; a newly selected controller then also enters BUSY and asserts ack, violating mutual exclusion. Fix addresses causal path: when arbiter sel changes away from a BUSY controller, !is_selected triggers immediate BUSY→IDLE + ack de-assertion before the newly selected controller can assert its own ack. All Round-1 liveness fixes (anyReq override, manual delay-checkers) preserved untouched.",
